The :00 decay is real, specific, and 73 days sits exactly on the threshold

Prompted by a challenge: I asserted decay from three bins without testing it,
and never asked whether 73 days can resolve anything at this dispersion. Both
now tested.

1. THE DECAY IS REAL - four independent checks agree

  trend slope, day-clustered   -0.1395 c/day, CI [-0.3069, +0.0154], P 0.0377
  constant-edge simulation     P(monotone decline this steep) = 0.0116
  split-point robustness       equal-trade thirds -8.49c, calendar thirds
                               -8.49c, halves -6.46c
  rolling 21-day window        monotone, no step

  2026-05-25  +8.82c win 0.8810      2026-07-06  +1.99c win 0.8112
  2026-06-08 +11.00c win 0.9008      2026-07-13  -0.98c win 0.7803
  2026-06-22  +8.62c win 0.8855      2026-07-20  -0.77c win 0.7822

The win rate falls from 88-90% to 78-81%: the outcome is changing, not the
price.

2. IT IS SPECIFIC TO :00, NOT A MARKET-WIDE DRIFT

  :00 strategy edge      -0.1395 c/day
  other-minute taker     +0.0541 c/day   (slightly RISING)
  all-market maker       +0.0086 c/day   (flat)

  :00 minus other-minute slope: -0.1936 c/day
  95% CI [-0.3444, -0.0561]   P(>=0) 0.0040

The rest of the market did not change. :00 decayed against it. That is the
signature of an edge being arbitraged away, not of a regime shift.

3. IS 73 DAYS ENOUGH? EXACTLY, WHICH IS THE PROBLEM

  per-trade SD 35.6c   per-DAY SD 16.7c   6.2 trades/day
  SE of the mean, day-clustered: 1.95c over 73 days
  smallest edge resolvable at 80% power:  5.47c
  observed full-sample edge:             +5.47c

The observed edge sits exactly on the detection threshold. 73 days was just
enough to catch the original effect and nowhere near enough to measure the
residual:

  confirm +7.50c    39 days
  confirm +5.00c    87 days
  confirm +2.76c   286 days (9.5 months)

Detecting the decay itself needed ~53 days split across periods, which is why
the arc is visible while the current level is not.

CONCLUSION. The :00 edge was real and large - about +9 to +11c through late
May and June at an 88-90% win rate - and decayed monotonically through July to
roughly zero, specifically, against a flat market. The strategy is not wrong
and the backtest is not broken; the edge was there and is now largely gone.
Anything priced off the full-sample +5.47c is priced off the part that has
already disappeared.

